@id n0_traveller
# DRAFT
# The traveller (Will Fuller) beside the porter on the carter's wagon, night 0. The carter has pulled in; as the cart with the dead comes close the traveller breaks off whatever he was saying (traveller_road.talk is that talk) and turns to it. It opens on him, not on a greeting: they have been talking all the way from the fields.
# Four pilgrims under sacking, found in the ditch: seven this month on this road. They went in at the abbey's gate to see the saint; nobody saw them come out; they turn up after, outside the walls.
# The ride reveals nothing of what or who is behind it: no demon, no men, no robbery. Only the dead, the count, the abbey, and a man too frightened to say what people say.
# If the porter told him he's the abbey's porter (n0_road_porter), he says your abbey; if not, the carter has told him. If he gave his name (n0_road_alric), Will uses it.
# If the cart broke in before Will gave his own name, he gives it as the cart goes (done_name: knows_traveller).
# He asks the porter one thing back: whether he'll still go in at that gate (n0_cart_go).
# One talk: the questions left come up again until all are asked; then he watches the cart go and closes it (done). What he doesn't get to say here (Aldgate may cut it short), the porter can ask him after (traveller_road.talk, after).
# Answer paths the tests take: test_prologue and test_flow answer 0 throughout (who, abbey, abbey_how, say, see, see_go, done). The two lines that open it ("Whoa. Look at that." and the cart going by) are checked word for word.
== start
Traveller {afraid}: Whoa. Look at that.
(The cart creaks by close enough to touch. Shapes lie under sacking on its bed, three side by side and one across them.)
Traveller {afraid, swallow}: God's wounds. That's not one man. That's four.
* God rest them. Who were they? -> who
* What happened to them? -> what
* (Cross yourself.) -> pray

== who [set n0_cart_who]
Traveller {sad}: Pilgrims, by the badges on their hats. Men who saved a year to see a saint, and nobody here to ask after them.
-> count

== what [set n0_cart_what]
Traveller {afraid, blink}: Found in the ditch, the carter says. All four in the one ditch, and not a mark on them.
-> count

== pray [set n0_cart_pray]
(You say the words for the dead under your breath. His lips move with yours.)
Traveller {grave}: Say one for yourself while you're at it.
-> count

== count
-> count_porter [if n0_road_porter]
-> count_plain

== count_porter
Traveller {grave}: That makes seven this month, on this road alone. Every one of them bound for your abbey, to see the saint.
-> rumour

== count_plain
Traveller {grave}: Seven this month, on this road alone. The carter says you're for the abbey in the lane. That's where they were all bound.
-> rumour

== rumour
-> done [if n0_cart_abbey] [if n0_cart_say] [if n0_cart_see]
-> rumour_ask

== rumour_ask
* [if not n0_cart_abbey] Why lay it at the abbey's door? -> abbey
* [if not n0_cart_say] What do people say? -> say
* [if not n0_cart_see] I'll see for myself what's there. -> see

== abbey [set n0_cart_abbey]
Traveller {afraid}: They go in at that gate to see the saint. Nobody sees them come out.
Traveller {grave}: Then a week on, a month on, they turn up in a ditch outside the walls. Like those.
* How? -> abbey_how
* (Say nothing.) -> rumour

== abbey_how
(He crosses himself.)
Traveller {afraid, swallow}: I don't say how. I don't know how. Nobody does.
-> rumour

== say [set n0_cart_say]
(He opens his mouth, and shuts it again.)
Traveller {afraid, blink}: People say a good many things, brother. None of them in daylight.
Traveller {afraid}: You'll hear it all at the Keys tonight. I'd rather not be the one who told you.
-> rumour

== see [set n0_cart_see]
Traveller {grave}: You will, brother. That's what worries me. Knowing that, you'll still go in at that gate?
* I'm sent. I'll go. -> see_go
* I don't know. -> see_unsure

== see_go [set n0_cart_go=yes]
Traveller {sad}: Sent. Aye. So were they, in their way.
-> rumour

== see_unsure [set n0_cart_go=unsure]
Traveller {grave}: That's the first wise thing anyone's said on this cart.
-> rumour

== done
(The cart's lantern goes small down the road behind you. He doesn't take his eyes off it.)
-> done_named [if n0_road_alric]
-> done_plain

== done_named
Traveller {sad}: God keep you better than He kept those, Brother Alric.
-> end

== done_plain
Traveller {sad}: God keep you better than He kept those, brother.
-> done_name [if not knows_traveller]
-> end

== done_name [set knows_traveller]
Traveller {sad, look down}: Will Fuller. A man should know who he saw that with.
-> end

== again
-> done [if n0_cart_abbey] [if n0_cart_say] [if n0_cart_see]
-> again_ask

== again_ask
Traveller {grave}: I can still see that cart, brother. Ask, if you want to.
-> rumour_ask

== leave
Traveller {sad}: Look away, then. I wish I could.
